---
// src/components/calculators/content/MulchContent.astro
import { mulchDimensions, getMulchMetrics } from '../../../data/mulch-dimensions';
---

<div class="calc-content-prose">
  <h2>How to Use the Mulch Calculator</h2>
  <p>
    Whether you are mulching a front walkway flower bed, bordering an entire backyard fence, or installing a playground safety cushion, calculating your mulch requirements accurately saves money and prevents wasted bags:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Enter Landscape Bed Dimensions:</strong> Input your bed length and width in feet or inches. For irregular free-form curving beds, split the area into approximate rectangles or use our <a href="/calculators/square-footage-calculator/">Square Footage Calculator</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Select Mulch Layer Depth:</strong> The recommended depth for new garden beds is <strong>3 inches</strong>. For annual spring color top-dressing, use <strong>1 to 2 inches</strong>. For commercial playground safety surfaces under play equipment, building safety guidelines recommend <strong>6 inches</strong> of compacted engineered wood fiber.</li>
    <li><strong>Choose Bagged vs. Bulk Delivery:</strong> For projects requiring under 2 cubic yards (~27 bags), buying bagged mulch at a local garden center is typically more economical and convenient. For projects requiring 3 or more cubic yards, bulk delivery saves money and labor.</li>
  </ol>

  <!-- Popular Mulch Sizes Grid -->
  <h2>Popular Mulch Bed Dimensions (Quick Reference Guides)</h2>
  <p>
    Working with standard landscape dimensions? Explore our exact-dimension calculation guides complete with bag counts (2 cu ft & 1.5 cu ft), bulk cubic yardage, and cost comparisons:
  </p>

  <div class="mulch-sizes-grid">
    {mulchDimensions.map((mulch) => {
      const m2 = getMulchMetrics(mulch.areaSqFt, 2);
      const m3 = getMulchMetrics(mulch.areaSqFt, 3);
      const anchorTitle = `${mulch.label} Bed (${m3.bags2cuft} Bags @ 3")`;
      return (
        <a
          href={`/calculators/mulch-calculator/${mulch.slug}/`}
          class="mulch-size-card"
          title={`Mulch calculator and bag chart for a ${mulch.label} bed`}
        >
          <div class="mulch-card-top">
            <span class="mulch-card-dim">{mulch.label}</span>
            <span class="mulch-card-sqft">{mulch.areaSqFt} sq ft</span>
          </div>
          <strong class="mulch-card-anchor">{anchorTitle}</strong>
          <p class="mulch-card-desc">{mulch.useCase}</p>
          <div class="mulch-card-footer">
            <span class="mulch-card-badge">{m2.bags2cuft} bags (2") • {m3.bags2cuft} bags (3")</span>
            <span class="mulch-card-cta">View Guide →</span>
          </div>
        </a>
      );
    })}
  </div>

  <h2>Common Landscape Bed Dimensions & Mulch Reference Table</h2>
  <p>
    Quick reference table showing square footage, bulk cubic yards, and 2-cubic-foot bags across 10 standard landscaping project sizes:
  </p>

  <div class="table-container">
    <table class="reference-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Bed Size (ft)</th>
          <th>Typical Application</th>
          <th>Area (sq ft)</th>
          <th>2" Depth (Bags)</th>
          <th>3" Depth (Bags)</th>
          <th>Bulk Volume (3")</th>
          <th>Bagged Cost ($4.25)</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {mulchDimensions.map((mulch) => {
          const m2 = getMulchMetrics(mulch.areaSqFt, 2);
          const m3 = getMulchMetrics(mulch.areaSqFt, 3);
          return (
            <tr>
              <td>
                <a href={`/calculators/mulch-calculator/${mulch.slug}/`} class="table-link">
                  <strong>{mulch.label}</strong>
                </a>
              </td>
              <td>{mulch.useCase}</td>
              <td>{mulch.areaSqFt} sq ft</td>
              <td>{m2.bags2cuft} bags ({m2.cuYds} yd³)</td>
              <td><strong>{m3.bags2cuft} bags</strong></td>
              <td>{m3.cuYds} yd³</td>
              <td>${m3.baggedCost}</td>
            </tr>
          );
        })}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Mulch Conversion Math: Bags to Cubic Yards</h2>
  <p>
    One cubic yard equals exactly 27 cubic feet. Because retail mulch is most commonly packaged in <strong>2.0 cubic foot bags</strong>:
  </p>
  <div class="formula-callout">
    <code>1 Cubic Yard = 27 cu ft ÷ 2.0 cu ft = 13.5 Bags</code>
  </div>
  <p>
    If purchasing smaller <strong>1.5 cubic foot bags</strong>, you need <strong>18 bags per cubic yard</strong> (27 ÷ 1.5).
  </p>

  <h2>When to Choose Bagged Mulch vs. Bulk Mulch</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Buy Bagged Mulch When (&lt; 3 Cubic Yards):</strong> If your garden bed requires fewer than 25 to 30 bags (under 2 yards), buying bagged mulch at a home improvement store is faster, simpler to stage directly around your garden beds without wheelbarrowing from the driveway, and avoids the $40 to $75 bulk delivery charge.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Order Bulk Mulch When (&ge; 3 Cubic Yards):</strong> For projects requiring 3 or more cubic yards, bulk delivery saves $50 to $200+ on material alone and eliminates dozens of heavy plastic bags that fill landfills. Make sure you have an accessible, flat driveway area where a dump truck can unload safely.
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>

<style>
  .mulch-sizes-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem;
  }

  .mulch-size-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    background: var(--color-surface, rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6));
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border, rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.15));
    border-radius: 12px;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
  }

  .mulch-size-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-accent, #38bdf8);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
  }

  .mulch-card-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .mulch-card-dim {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--color-heading, #ffffff);
  }

  .mulch-card-sqft {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-accent, #38bdf8);
    background: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.1);
    padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 9999px;
  }

  .mulch-card-anchor {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-accent, #38bdf8);
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .mulch-card-desc {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-muted, #94a3b8);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    flex-grow: 1;
  }

  .mulch-card-footer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding-top: 0.75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border, rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.1));
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .mulch-card-badge {
    color: var(--color-muted, #94a3b8);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .mulch-card-cta {
    color: var(--color-accent, #38bdf8);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .table-container {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border, rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.15));
    border-radius: 10px;
  }

  .reference-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .reference-table th {
    background: rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.8);
    color: var(--color-heading, #ffffff);
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border, rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.2));
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .reference-table td {
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border, rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.1));
    color: var(--color-text, #cbd5e1);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .reference-table tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .table-link {
    color: var(--color-accent, #38bdf8);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .table-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .formula-callout {
    background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);
    border: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.3);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent, #38bdf8);
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
  }

  .formula-callout code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, monospace);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #38bdf8;
  }
</style>
